#hash((content-digest . "0aa98f48ca62a6cb75d5aaa2f6cd2f2c7dd9f02456c04042fc2910c76d6836f5") (milestone . 896) (plan-id . "fb67e0429ed155a4b4e3f31afe3ef3ca7748ee891c06247b11e5e2a86cfebd75") (report . "Four rounds were completed and all four returned CHANGES-REQUESTED. All 33 findings were reproduced against the tree before any fix was written, and every one is fixed with its own evidence: the W2 gate repair carries a red-first capture showing the previously masked failure now reaches the gate, the prose corrections are diffs against the artifacts they cite, and the two round-3 substantiation findings are re-measurements rather than restatements - the sweep was genuinely re-run and the checksums genuinely re-verified in full. The pattern across the rounds is consistent: each round found the same class of defect one step further along, in the claim that pointed at the evidence rather than in the evidence itself, which is why rounds 2 and 3 returned findings of the same shape as round 1's. Round 4 is the informative one for what this wave actually was: it found no new defect in the W7 content and six new defects in the evidence, three of them the same trap it had been used to catch - a detector that mistakes a green summary line for a failure, a stale enumeration, and a caveat that contradicts the artifact it introduces. Every round so far has found the same shape of thing one step further along, in the claim that pointed at the evidence rather than in the evidence, and the reason is structural rather than bad luck: a committed artifact names the tree it ran on, so every artifact-only commit moves the ground under the sentence that cites it. A further round is outstanding. That sentence is deliberately phrased without a round number: the previous two revisions of it each named a specific round and were therefore stale at the commit that carried them, because the fix and the recording of the round it referred to landed in the same commit. A pending-round claim that cannot fall behind is worth more than one that reads precisely and is wrong. No value in this record is invented, and this record does not assert approval. One further finding, R4-F7, was surfaced by the round-5 reviewer in the seconds before it hit its quota and is recorded here: the sweep had been run with the wrong instrument entirely, so two of its nineteen greens were vacuous. That makes 24 findings across four rounds, and it is the clearest statement of this wave's shape - the same trap caught at successively lower levels, until the level reached was the instrument itself. Round 5 reviewed at b9a0ac1ad through zai-coding-plan/glm-5.3-flash and returned CHANGES-REQUESTED: the validation record's eight duplicated top-level keys, under which the values the gate reads were a stale block naming a superseded head. The reviewer believed the record was unparseable; it was instead silently stale, which is worse - it read cleanly and would have failed the gate. Running the gate the way CI does then surfaced four more real defects the reviewer, having no shell, could not see: two missing gate-required fields, a mismatched implementation-sha, and a remaining-items vocabulary the gate does not accept. That is 33 findings across five rounds, and the shape has now repeated at every level this wave has touched: a check that passes is not a check that ran, and a record that reads is not a record that is accepted. That was 33 findings across five rounds. Round 6 added seven more, five of them stale summary fields in these very records and two of them regressions from the round-5 remediation itself, making 40 across six rounds. The shape has repeated at every level this wave has touched: a check that passes is not a check that ran, a record that reads is not a record that is accepted, and a field that has been rebound is not a field that has been described. Round 7 then showed the same thing one level up: the fixes for the stale-count class were themselves stale by construction, because each was written in the same commit that recorded the round it described. That is three consecutive rounds in which a hand-written enumeration - a delta, a manifest total, a review count - was wrong at the head carrying it, and the pattern is now the finding rather than any single instance. The counts in the sibling records have been removed rather than updated, and the count in this record's verdict is derived from the findings it contains.") (reviewed-sha . "4891dd2a52007053e9af7eea0b508bc0e548fcb0") (reviewer . "independent read-only VERIFY subagents (reviewer role), 5 rounds solicited") (rounds . (#hash((findings . (#hash((id . "R1-F1") (resolution . "FIXED. The W2 checks are now a test-suite run through run-tests whose returned failure count drives (exit 1), so failed-result? sees a non-zero exit. The W2 overlap review and SHA256SUMS are pinned to the frozen v1.00.29 campaign; the W0 ownership matrix stays derived so the checks double as a live drift check (both matrices have identical overlap scope: 34 platform/fast, 46 security/fast). Red-first proof at raw/red-first-worker-security-w2.txt: with the W2 path pointed at a nonexistent directory the file now exits 1 and the runner reports FAILED, where the identical broken state before the fix reported PASSED (33/33, exit 0).") (severity . "blocking") (summary . "tests/test-worker-security.rkt derived its W2 overlap artifact paths from q-version (naming artifacts/tier-ownership/v1.00.31-w2, which does not exist) and could not fail the gate, so the regression was invisible")) #hash((id . "R1-F2") (resolution . "FIXED. CHANGELOG and the release report name the matrix's actual values and say why they moved (the bake's own derivation sweep changed two of the nine digest-bound inputs, so the matrix was regenerated by its canonical generator).") (severity . "blocking") (summary . "W6 PERMANENT prose bound the verdict to the superseded rehearsal identity (head fc1a6fa36, inputs digest a1b99fe2) while the committed matrix records 50bdf7334 / fb224a6f")) #hash((id . "R1-F3") (resolution . "FIXED. Both passages now state six of seven gates pass and that readiness is deferred, not passed, with the reason (branch-gated; its .gate-evidence records must name the release commit and version).") (severity . "blocking") (summary . "The changelog claimed every release-preflight gate passes locally and listed readiness among them, while release-preflight.json records readiness as deferred-by-design")) #hash((id . "R1-F4") (resolution . "PARTIALLY FIXED in round 1, completed in round 3. The checksum step was corrected to run from the repo root and a single capture retained per gate; head coherence is stated precisely rather than claimed. Round 3 judged the form correct but the substantiation incomplete, which became R3-F4.") (severity . "blocking") (summary . "W7 evidence was not coherently bound: the preflight named the first bake commit, the preflight JSON a later commit, and the verify chain an intermediate one, and that chain recorded a failed checksum run caused by executing sha256sum -c from inside the artifact directory")))) (reviewed-sha . "55abf0271f61ae4797881c64d3948834cc5c1d7e") (round . 1) (verdict . "CHANGES-REQUESTED")) #hash((findings . (#hash((id . "R2-F1") (resolution . "FIXED. The entry now records both re-stamps and names the current committed values as authoritative.") (severity . "blocking") (summary . "w4-recovery.json still described the W6 matrix as re-stamped to fc1a6fa36 with byte-identical inputs, contradicting the regeneration this bake performed")) #hash((id . "R2-F2") (resolution . "PARTIALLY FIXED in round 2, completed in round 3. The report was corrected to the then-current preflight head, but round 3 found the same class of defect one step further along: the preflight was later re-run at b0f19d6bd while the report and the validation record still said 58d302db. Both now name b0f19d6bd, the head the retained capture names.") (severity . "blocking") (summary . "The release report quoted the first bake commit fcfa9ab3 and 84 changed .rkt files while the retained preflight capture recorded a later commit and 93")) #hash((id . "R2-F3") (resolution . "FIXED. The 1511 value is consistent across the report, the preflight JSON, the validation record and the chain capture.") (severity . "blocking") (summary . "The report quoted 1510 test files scanned for the version-expectation lint; the real count is 1511")) #hash((id . "R2-F4") (resolution . "FIXED. The claim is replaced by the precise account: each capture names the tree it ran against; the commits between the suite chain (e9af72fee) and the content head change only docs/reports prose and this directory's own JSON and raw captures, which no test reads; and git diff --name-only e9af72fee..86002515f confirms no source or test file changed after the chain ran, so the chain's numbers describe the merge candidate's code.") (severity . "blocking") (summary . "release-preflight.json claimed the three captures were 'all bound to the same content head', which was false - a committed artifact cannot contain the SHA of the commit that carries it")))) (reviewed-sha . "21b753a26595be03db432f8a046efd0a97a6876a") (round . 2) (verdict . "CHANGES-REQUESTED")) #hash((findings . (#hash((id . "R3-F1") (resolution . "FIXED. Both now name b0f19d6bd.") (severity . "blocking") (summary . "The release report and the validation record still attributed the preflight to 58d302db while the retained preflight artifacts (release-preflight.json and raw/preflight-locally-runnable.txt) both record b0f19d6bd. The previous fix had chased the moving commit one step and stopped short.")) #hash((id . "R3-F2") (resolution . "FIXED. The sweep was re-run at the final head - 19 files, 0 failures, 0 errors - and the new capture states in its own header what it supersedes and why. The reviewer also observed that raco test exits 0 even when a case fails, so the per-file rackunit counts rather than the exit code are the signal; that is recorded in the preflight JSON, and it is the same failure mode that hid the worker-security W2 regression.") (severity . "blocking") (summary . "release-preflight.json claimed 0 failures, 0 errors citing raw/version-derivation-tests.log, but that capture was taken mid-repair and records test-wave-integrity-adversarial.rkt red (1/8) while the W6 matrix was still pinned to the pre-regeneration identity. The claim was true and the evidence under it was not.")) #hash((id . "R3-F3") (resolution . "FIXED. Head, counts and elapsed time now match the capture they cite; the fast-suite duration (20m51s to 20m53s) was corrected in the same pass, and a raw-captures block now names which file substantiates which number.") (severity . "moderate") (summary . "The validation record quoted a full regression at 1935c2c90 with 20548 of 20549 tests and 29m40s while citing raw/verify-chain.txt, which records e9af72fee with 20553 of 20554 and 29m36s - an earlier run's numbers under a later run's filename.")) #hash((id . "R3-F4") (resolution . "FIXED. The full unfiltered per-manifest output is retained in the chain capture: 6/6 W6, 9/9 W7, 1/1 tier-ownership, 16/16 entries, run from the repository root. It is retained there rather than in a sidecar log because the artifact-provenance linter requires every file under the wave artifact directory to be bound by SHA256SUMS. The single unavoidable self-reference is stated in the log, the report and the preflight JSON: the manifest entry for the log covers the log including the checksum section, so the log cannot verify its own entry.") (severity . "moderate") (summary . "The chain's checksum section showed three OK lines for manifests holding sixteen entries, so its all-OK summary was unsubstantiated by its own excerpt.")) #hash((id . "R3-NB") (resolution . "Accepted as accurate. The 1510 in the red-first capture is labelled rather than edited, because rewriting a red-first capture to match a later run would destroy the red/green pair it exists to record. The reviewer independently confirmed sound: the runner base-dir tests (non-vacuous, each building a decoy q/ fixture, and now counted by the runner), all eight frozen-path pins and both authoring-identity pins with truthful comments, the readiness-deferred wording, the W6 PERMANENT and W4 DELIVERED bounding, the absence of any PR-check substitution, and the playwright-sidecar environmental claim (@requires browser at the file, ci profile skips it, identical failure on main).") (severity . "non-blocking") (summary . "Round 3's non-blocking observations: the superseded red-first capture's 1510 count, a confusing runner taxonomy label in the W2 red-first record, and prose drift in one suite duration.")) #hash((id . "R3-TOOL") (resolution . "Recorded so the round's scope is not overstated. Its findings were all verified independently against the tree before any fix was written, and all four were real.") (severity . "process") (summary . "Round 3 ran without an exec tool in the child process, so it could not recompute the content digest, run git diff, verify checksums or execute tests, and marked those unverified.")))) (reviewed-sha . "9ff617f2c73f7207fd6fd73077b16dcfd3996823 (chain head e9af72fee)") (round . 3) (rounds-prior-fix-check . "Six of the eight prior findings confirmed GENUINELY FIXED: R1-F1 (the W2 checks now run through run-tests whose failure count drives the exit; the frozen v1.00.29 artifacts verified on disk and self-identifying; the red-first capture consistent at 33-before/38-after with exactly the three artifact-reading cases failing), R1-F2 (the strict-runner assertion now requires both the strict variable and a run-tests.rkt invocation, checked against ci.yml's fast, platform and security windows; a lane dropping strictness cannot satisfy it), R1-F3 (no stale fc1a6fa36/a1b99fe2 identity survives in the release surface - the remaining mentions are legitimate history), R2-F1 (w4-recovery.json records both re-stamps and matches the committed matrix field-for-field), R2-F3 (1511 everywhere in the release surface), and R1-F4's checksum path. R1-F4 was accepted as fixed in form but left substantiation incomplete, which became R3-F4. R2-F2 was judged NOT FIXED and became R3-F1.") (verdict . "CHANGES-REQUESTED")) #hash((additional-finding . #hash((attribution . "Found by the round-5 reviewer in the seconds before it hit its quota; the reviewer died before it could write this up, so the finding was reconstructed from its output and then verified directly against the tree by running the sweep both ways. Recorded against round 4 because round 5 never completed.") (id . "R4-F7") (resolution . "FIXED by re-measurement with the correct instrument. The sweep now runs racket scripts/run-tests.rkt per file - the runner whose exit code reporting.rkt actually gates on - and reports 376 tests, 376 passed, 0 failed, 0 timeouts, every file exit 0, and 0 files with no test count. The capture carries the runner's own Tests:/Files: lines and each exit code, so a vacuous green is detectable rather than assumed absent, and its header records the full instrument history including that a fourth false alarm came from the capture script's own detector grepping for raco test's summary shape instead of the runner's. This is the same trap as R1-F1 and R4-F1, caught a third time and finally at the level of the instrument itself.") (severity . "blocking") (summary . "The wrong instrument. The 19-file sweep that substantiates release-preflight.json's 0-failures claim was run with bare raco test, which is wrong twice over: it exits 0 even when a case fails, and for a file whose entry point is module+ main rather than module+ test it executes nothing and still exits 0. Two of the 19 files are shaped that way - test-deterministic-clock.rkt (10 cases) and test-wave-delivery-integrity-register.rkt (10 cases) - so their greens were vacuous: a pass that ran zero tests. The capture recorded zero lines of output for exactly those two files, which is what finally exposed it."))) (findings . (#hash((id . "R4-F1") (resolution . "FIXED, by re-measurement rather than by editing the capture. This is the raco-test-exits-0 trap reproduced one level down, in the very tool written to catch it. Re-run with a detector that requires a non-zero failure or error count: 0 of 19, agreeing with the per-file counts above the footer. The re-run also disclosed a second bug of its own - EXIT= was reading echo's status rather than raco's - so the exit code is now captured from the command directly. The capture names both superseded captures and why each is superseded.") (severity . "blocking") (summary . "The 19-file sweep capture's footer said 11 of 19 files with a reported failure while every per-file section above it read 0 failures and 0 errors. The detector matched rackunit's green 0 failure(s) summary line. The capture is SHA256SUMS-bound and is cited by the report, the preflight JSON and the validation record as the substantiation of 0 failures, 0 errors, so on its face it contradicted the claim it was cited for.")) #hash((id . "R4-F2") (resolution . "FIXED. The block now quotes the actual diff: twelve paths, none under tests/, scripts/, util/, extensions/, ci/ or .github/, which is the claim that matters - no source or test file changed after the chain ran.") (severity . "moderate") (summary . "The validation record's head-coherence block quoted a git diff enumeration of the e9af72fee delta that predated the sweep capture and therefore omitted a file that had changed. The log's own header names a head and a timestamp later than the chain, which is proof enough that the enumeration was stale.")) #hash((id . "R4-F3") (resolution . "FIXED. The line is repointed at the checksum section that does exist, and the live re-check script was repointed at /tmp so it cannot reintroduce an unbound file into the wave artifact directory.") (severity . "moderate") (summary . "The chain's summary line still pointed at raw/checksums-final.txt, the sidecar design abandoned because the artifact-provenance linter requires every wave artifact to be bound by SHA256SUMS. The named file was never committed.")) #hash((id . "R4-F4") (resolution . "FIXED. The challenge was upheld: the caveat described a mechanism that was not the one in play. The actual order is write the section, bind the manifest over the finalized log, then re-run the verification, so the line is true of the committed bytes. Reworded in the log, the report and the preflight JSON, and sha256sum -c confirmed 16/16 at this commit. The reviewer's inability to hash the file - it had no exec tool - is why the question needed settling by running the command rather than by reading it.") (severity . "moderate") (summary . "The self-reference caveat said the log could not contain the verification of its own entry, while the retained output immediately below contains exactly the verify-chain.txt: OK line - the caveat contradicted the artifact it introduced.")) #hash((id . "R4-F5") (resolution . "ACCEPTED AS NON-BLOCKING, deliberately not fixed. It is a warning-level convention and the file is classified and counted correctly by the runner - the fast suite is 1209 = W4's 1208 plus this file, and its four cases are green in the sweep capture. Touching a test file after the chain ran would invalidate the head-coherence claim that no test file changed since e9af72fee, so fixing a cosmetic tag would have cost the coherence guarantee that every other finding in this wave was about. Recorded as a follow-up instead of traded against that guarantee.") (severity . "minor") (summary . "tests/test-runner-base-dir-resolution.rkt carries no @suite/@speed metadata, which the schema treats as required. The runner's own accounting records metadata-completeness=explicit:0/heuristic:0/missing:1 for the file, so the gap is measured rather than inferred. It is the only new test file deviating from the convention. Neither of lint-all's two warnings is about this file; they are arch and release-readiness, both pre-existing and non-blocking.")) #hash((id . "R4-F6") (resolution . "FIXED, and then superseded in substance by R4-F7. The report no longer describes the file set in prose at all: it now states the sweep's real totals (376 tests across the 19 files) measured through the project runner, which is the thing the sentence was trying to establish.") (severity . "minor") (summary . "The release report's set arithmetic named a second new runner test that is not among the 19 files in the sweep.")) #hash((id . "R4-HYG") (resolution . "FIXED. The chain log is untracked, .chainlogs/ is now in .gitignore with the reason recorded, and nul is untracked. Both were removed from the index only; no file was deleted from the working tree, and the pre-existing root script w1-apply-covers.py was left in place as out of scope for this wave.") (severity . "moderate") (summary . "Artifact hygiene, found while verifying the findings above: .chainlogs/w7-version-derive-tests.log was tracked, which this campaign forbids outright, and the repository root carried a stray file named nul containing the shell error /bin/sh: 1: where: not found - accidental redirection output, tracked since v1.00.04.")) #hash((id . "R4-NB") (resolution . "Accepted and recorded as a follow-up for the next wave. The W2 suite that R1-F1 was about is airtight, so the finding does not reopen it; the main suite is a pre-existing property the validation record already classifies as follow-up work.") (severity . "non-blocking") (summary . "Round 4 also noted that the worker-security main suite (33 cases) still discards the value of its own (run-tests suite) call, so a main-suite failure cannot reach the exit code. It judged the W2 suite - the R1-F1 subject - airtight and the gap out of W7 scope.")) #hash((id . "R4-TOOL") (resolution . "Recorded so the round's scope is not overstated. Every finding was independently verified against the tree, and the one that hinged on execution, R4-F4, was settled by running sha256sum -c rather than by reading. The reviewer judged the twelve prior fixes from file contents alone and was correct on all twelve.") (severity . "process") (summary . "Round 4 ran without an exec tool, so the content digest, record-commit, verify, all three checksum manifests, every git diff claim and all test executions were unverified by the reviewer and marked as such.")))) (reviewed-sha . "2428611c392f0feec595c3e881beb88536ca52c6 (the content head when round 4 ran; the commit recording it, 697135ca, rebinds the trio to this head)") (round . 4) (rounds-prior-fix-check . "All twelve prior findings confirmed GENUINELY FIXED. R3-F2 was accepted as substantively fixed but its replacement capture introduced a new defect, which became R4-F1. R3-F4 was accepted as fixed in substance with its self-reference caveat upheld, which became R4-F4. R3-F1 was confirmed fixed, with the reviewer judging the residual gap between b0f19d6bd and the content head to be the unavoidable an-artifact-names-the-tree-it-ran-on consequence rather than the same defect, but noting the validation record's enumeration of that gap was incomplete, which became R4-F2.") (verdict . "CHANGES-REQUESTED")) #hash((findings . (#hash((id . "R5-F1") (resolution . "FIXED. The stale block is gone: 27 top-level pairs, 27 unique keys, zero duplicates, rebuilt through Racket's own writer so neither duplicates nor malformed structure can survive. implementation-sha now equals the evidence record's, so the gate's cross-record comparison passes. Verified by running the real gate the way CI runs it: eight structural rejections before the fix, two after, and the two remaining are the legitimate pending-review blocks. Four further defects surfaced by running that gate are recorded as R5-F1b through R5-F1e.") (severity . "blocking") (summary . "The validation record carried eight duplicated top-level keys, and the values the wave gate consumes were a stale trailing block naming content head 86002515 instead of b9a0ac1ad. The reviewer's stated mechanism - that Racket's reader rejects duplicate keys, leaving the record unparseable - is incorrect, and the true mechanism is worse. Racket does not reject duplicate keys in a #hasheq literal: it silently keeps the last. So the record read cleanly, reported 25 unique keys, and passed every structural check, while the gate compared the stale implementation-sha against the evidence record's and would have failed. The reviewer correctly identified the blocking consequence and the stale head; only the mechanism, and therefore the fix, differ.")) #hash((id . "R5-F1b") (resolution . "FIXED. implementation-sha is 3a3d3297fe5172c26303a159a67a187e4639a459, matching the evidence record and the head-coherence text in the same datum.") (severity . "blocking") (summary . "implementation-sha named 86002515f9de49d4abd83d83fd279656ab7c15e7, a superseded content head, while the same record's head-coherence text and the other two records named b9a0ac1ad. The gate requires validation's implementation-sha to equal the evidence record's, so this alone would have been rejected - pointing at a field whose stale value was itself an artifact of the duplicate-key shadowing.")) #hash((id . "R5-F1c") (resolution . "FIXED, both with measurements taken at this head rather than quoted. format-compile: raco make and raco fmt canonicality (the same test scripts/pre-commit.rkt performs) over all 29 changed .rkt files between base 50bdf7334 and this head - 29 compiled, 29 canonical, 0 not-canonical, 0 fmt-error. fast: promoted to the top level from suites.fast, with its provenance noted. The nested copy is retained so the record still shows where the number came from.") (severity . "blocking") (summary . "The record had no top-level format-compile field and no top-level fast field, both required by the gate's validation-required-fields and both then validated for a passed result. The fast measurement existed but only nested under suites, which the gate does not consult - so the record carried a true number in a place no gate would ever read it.")) #hash((id . "R5-F1d") (resolution . "FIXED without flattening away the meaning. The first item is genuinely deferred by design and is now classified deferred-noncritical; the other four are noncritical. Each keeps its original descriptive classification in a new label field, so nothing descriptive is lost and the gate sees the vocabulary it requires.") (severity . "blocking") (summary . "The five remaining-items used descriptive classifications - deferred-by-design, environmental-not-a-regression, follow-up-not-blocking, verdict-bounded, outstanding-coordinator-owned - none of which valid-noncritical-remaining-item? accepts. That predicate admits exactly noncritical and deferred-noncritical. The items were truthful and each carried a nonempty owner and rationale; only the vocabulary was wrong, so the gate rejected the whole list.")) #hash((id . "R5-F1e") (resolution . "FIXED; recorded here as the provenance of R5-F1b through R5-F1d, which were found by running the gate rather than by reading the record. The lesson is this wave's recurring one, one level up again: a check that passes is not a check that ran. The record satisfied every read-based inspection available to a reviewer without a shell, and was simultaneously rejected by the project's own gate. A reviewer without exec can confirm a record is well-formed; it cannot confirm a record is accepted.") (severity . "blocking") (summary . "The round-5 reviewer had no exec tool, so five of the eight gate rejections were invisible to it. Running the gate the way CI does surfaced them: the missing format-compile and fast fields, the implementation-sha mismatch, and the remaining-items vocabulary. Each is a real defect that would have failed CI's evidence gate on the merge candidate.")) #hash((id . "R5-F2") (resolution . "FIXED. Round 4's reviewed-sha is 2428611c392f0feec595c3e881beb88536ca52c6, with a note that this is the head when it ran. Worth stating plainly: this was the head-attribution defect class reintroduced while remediating that same class, by rebinding the trio and letting the head field follow the new binding instead of the review that actually happened.") (severity . "moderate") (summary . "Round 4's reviewed-sha had been rewritten to b9a0ac1ad7771306cda061a3ca4e9a4d3ee29278, a commit created at 01:31:48 local, thirty-nine minutes after the 00:52:24 commit that recorded round 4. The head round 4 reviewed was 2428611c3. Rounds 1 through 3 each keep their true head; round 4 was the only one that did not.")) #hash((id . "R5-F3") (resolution . "FIXED. Both say nineteen, matching the round-4 tally of 4 + 4 + 4 + 7 and the record's own verdict line.") (severity . "minor") (summary . "Two sentences still said eighteen findings where the record enumerates nineteen: the report field and round 5's note. Both undercount the set round 5 was instructed to confirm.")) #hash((id . "R5-F4") (resolution . "FIXED. The claim now states the real scope: the twelve paths, enumerated, with the reason no test reads any of them.") (severity . "minor") (summary . "release-preflight.json describes the post-preflight commits as changing only docs/reports/*.md prose and this directory's own JSON captures. The wave's current enumeration lists twelve paths including .gitignore, a deleted chain log, SHA256SUMS, raw .txt and .log captures and the three .rktd records - and the *.md glob does not match .rktd at all. A stale enumeration of exactly the kind fixed as R4-F2, surviving in a checksum-bound artifact.")) #hash((id . "R5-F5") (resolution . "FIXED. The raw index now lists all six bound raw captures.") (severity . "minor") (summary . "The same JSON's raw index lists five files but omits raw/red-first-worker-security-w2.txt, which its own independent-review text cites and which SHA256SUMS binds. An incomplete enumeration in a bound artifact - the standard R4-F2 enforced.")))) (note . "Round 5 ran to completion and returned CHANGES-REQUESTED with five findings, all reproduced against the tree and all fixed. It reviewed at b9a0ac1ad, the content head current when it ran. The reviewer had no exec tool and worked from the worktree's git metadata and the retained artifacts; everything checkable by reading, it checked, and the substantive test evidence - the 376-test sweep, the playwright failure's honest description, the head-coherence claim, and the R4-F5 trade-off - survived its attack. It judged the R4-F5 deferral legitimate rather than an evasion: the missing metadata is measured, the file's four tests are green, and editing a test file after the chain would have destroyed the no-test-file-changed guarantee the rest of the record depends on. Its one blocking finding was correct in substance and wrong in mechanism, and the correction mattered: the validation record was not unparseable but silently stale, a harder failure to notice and a more dangerous one to ship.") (reviewed-sha . "b9a0ac1ad7771306cda061a3ca4e9a4d3ee29278") (reviewer . "zai-coding-plan/glm-5.3-flash (independent, read-only)") (round . 5) (verdict . "CHANGES-REQUESTED")) #hash((findings . (#hash((id . "R6-F1") (resolution . "FIXED. Round 5's reviewed-sha is b9a0ac1ad7771306cda061a3ca4e9a4d3ee29278, the head it actually ran at. R5-F2's subject is restored to b9a0ac1ad with the interval corrected from forty minutes to the thirty-nine minutes the reflogs give. The lesson is recorded rather than quietly fixed: rebinding a record and letting a head field follow the new binding, instead of the event the field describes, is now a named failure mode of this wave.") (severity . "moderate") (summary . "A regression introduced by the round-5 remediation itself: the bulk head substitution rewrote text inside findings that are historical descriptions. R5-F2's subject, the SHA wrongly written into round 4's reviewed-sha, became the current head while its timestamps still described the old one, and round 5's own reviewed-sha was rewritten to a commit created hours after round 5 ran. Two commits apart this is the head-attribution class this record exists to police, reintroduced by the act of rebinding - the third occurrence in this wave, after R1-F4 and R2-F4.")) #hash((id . "R6-F2") (resolution . "FIXED against the measured delta. git diff --name-only b0f19d6bd..9841fed8 is ELEVEN paths, and the field now enumerates exactly those eleven. This is the R5-F4 class reintroduced by the R5-F4 fix - the third round running that a corrected enumeration was itself wrong.") (severity . "moderate") (summary . "The preflight JSON's chain enumeration said twelve paths and then named fourteen, and three of the files it named do not appear in that range at all because they predate the preflight head, while the deleted .chainlogs/w7-version-derive-tests.log does. Count and enumeration could not both be true, from the committed text alone.")) #hash((id . "R6-F3") (resolution . "FIXED by producing the captures rather than softening the claim. format-compile was re-measured at this head and retained as raw/format-compile-canonicality.txt: raco make and raco fmt canonicality over all 29 changed .rkt files, 29 compiled, 29 canonical, 0 not-canonical, 0 fmt-error, one line per file. focused-tests was re-measured through the project runner and retained as raw/focused-release-tests.txt: 8 files, 164 tests, 164 passed, 0 failed, every RUNNER-EXIT 0, the W7-touched four contributing 55 and the release-surface four the other 109. Both are bound in SHA256SUMS and indexed in the preflight JSON. A capture script written during this fix repeated the wave's signature error, taking the exit status after a pipe instead of from the command, which is why the capture records RUNNER-EXIT taken directly.") (severity . "minor") (summary . "The validation notes claimed every number in the record was retained as a raw capture, which was not true: the format-compile figures and both focused-tests figures had no capture behind them at all. The numbers were genuine but the unconditional claim overstated them.")) #hash((id . "R6-F4") (resolution . "FIXED. The notes now state five completed rounds, thirty-three findings, a seventh outstanding, and give round 4's composition accurately, including the tooling note and the two hygiene findings the F-numbered count omits.") (severity . "minor") (summary . "The validation notes still described four completed review rounds, a fifth outstanding and nineteen findings, at a head where five rounds had completed with thirty-three findings. It also described round 4 as having six findings while the breakdown it gave sums to five.")) #hash((id . "R6-F5") (resolution . "FIXED. The status now says five rounds and thirty-three findings. Its second half, that the wave is not merge-authorized while no APPROVED verdict exists, remains true and is unchanged.") (severity . "minor") (summary . "The evidence record's status still said four CHANGES-REQUESTED rounds with nineteen findings fixed, contradicting the review record it points at.")) #hash((id . "R6-F6") (resolution . "FIXED. The report says round 6 is pending and the timestamp now includes the round-5 entry with its reviewer.") (severity . "minor") (summary . "The review record's report field said Round 5 is pending and its timestamp key listed only r1 through r4, both contradicting the rounds list in the same record.")) #hash((id . "R6-F7") (resolution . "FIXED. The field now distinguishes the failed first attempt, which produced no verdict, from the round 5 that subsequently ran to completion on zai-coding-plan/glm-5.3-flash.") (severity . "minor") (summary . "The tooling-notes field said round 5 could not run because every route was quota-exhausted, contradicting the completed round-5 entry in the same record. The sentence was true of the first attempt when written and was never updated after that round completed on a different route.")))) (note . "Round 6 ran to completion and returned CHANGES-REQUESTED with seven findings, all reproduced against the tree and all fixed. Its distinctive property is that five of the seven were stale summary fields in the evidence records themselves, and two of those five were regressions introduced by the round-5 remediation: the bulk head substitution rewrote historical subjects, and a corrected enumeration was itself wrong. Every substantive piece of test evidence survived again - the 376-test sweep, the eleven-path delta, the honest description of the Playwright failure, and the remaining-items labels that preserve meaning alongside the gate vocabulary. The reviewer judged the format-compile and fast fields honestly labelled rather than dressed up, and judged the remaining-items fix as preserving meaning rather than flattening it. Its one substantive complaint was that two numbers in the validation record had no retained capture, which was correct, and is fixed by producing them.") (reviewed-sha . "9841fed8f2e24bb343e54d310ff836044a903602") (reviewer . "zai-coding-plan/glm-5.3-flash (independent, read-only)") (round . 6) (verdict . "CHANGES-REQUESTED")) #hash((findings . (#hash((id . "R7-F1") (resolution . "FIXED by removing the round number rather than updating it. The sentence now says a further round is outstanding, and states why it is phrased that way: the previous two revisions each named a specific round and were stale at the commit carrying them, because the fix and the recording of the round it referenced landed together. A pending-round claim that cannot fall behind is worth more than one that reads precisely and is wrong.") (severity . "minor") (summary . "The review record's report field said Round 6 is pending, in the same commit whose rounds list contained a completed round-6 entry and whose verdict said round 7 PENDING. R6-F6 had flagged the identical sentence one round earlier when it said Round 5 is pending; the fix moved the stale claim forward one round instead of eliminating it.")) #hash((id . "R7-F2") (resolution . "FIXED structurally rather than by editing the number. The status no longer restates a round or finding count at all: it states that the wave is verified through every round recorded in the review record, that all returned CHANGES-REQUESTED with every finding reproduced before being fixed, and that the counts live in the review record where they are derived from the findings it contains. Nothing here can fall behind.") (severity . "minor") (summary . "The evidence record's status said five CHANGES-REQUESTED rounds with thirty-three findings fixed, at a commit where the review record it points at read six rounds and forty findings. R6-F5 had established this exact class and the fix set the value one round behind by construction.")) #hash((id . "R7-F3") (resolution . "FIXED the same way as R7-F2. The leading count is gone; the field states that every recorded round completed and returned CHANGES-REQUESTED, and points at the review record for the derived counts.") (severity . "minor") (summary . "The validation record's notes opened by claiming five completed rounds and thirty-three findings, contradicted two sentences later in the same field by its own round-6 and seventh-round sentences and by the verdict's six and forty.")) #hash((id . "R7-F4") (resolution . "FIXED and re-measured. The totals are now 6/6 W6, 11/11 W7, 1/1 tier-ownership, 18/18 in total, in the release report and in the preflight JSON, each noting that the earlier figures are superseded and why the manifest grew. Verified by running sha256sum -c from the repository root against all three manifests: 11 + 6 + 1 = 18 OK. The bound historical capture raw/verify-chain.txt still says nine of nine and is left alone: it records what was true when it ran.") (severity . "moderate") (summary . "Stale manifest totals. The W7 manifest grew from nine to eleven entries when the round-6 remediation added the two captures, so the release report and the preflight JSON still claimed 9/9 W7 and 16/16 in total, false at the commit carrying them and inconsistent with the same JSON's own eight-entry raw index.")) #hash((id . "R7-F5") (resolution . "FIXED by measuring the range that matters rather than the one that existed when the field was written. git diff --name-only b0f19d6bd..3a3d3297f is THIRTEEN paths, and the field now enumerates exactly those thirteen. The three earlier wrong revisions are named in the field, because the pattern is the finding: a prose enumeration of a git delta, restated by hand at a head it does not describe.") (severity . "moderate") (summary . "The chain enumeration retained a stale present-tense twelve paths and corrected only to the pre-remediation endpoint 9841fed8f, so no stated count matched the range the merge candidate actually spans. This is the third consecutive round in which a corrected enumeration was itself stale at the head carrying it.")) #hash((id . "R7-F6") (resolution . "FIXED against the measured delta: git diff --name-only e9af72fee..3a3d3297f is fourteen paths, and the field now says fourteen. Same class as R7-F5 - an enumeration not maintained when the captures were added.") (severity . "moderate") (summary . "The validation record's head-coherence said the delta from the chain head lists twelve paths; the two round-6 captures make it fourteen at the named endpoint.")) #hash((id . "R7-F7") (resolution . "FIXED by naming the head the captures actually ran at, in the format-compile details and in both raw-captures entries, and by noting that no .rkt file changed since so the result describes this head's code while the capture keeps its own. The notes sentence now says each capture names the head it ran on rather than claiming a re-measurement at the binding head. This is the campaign's own rule, restated after being broken: a committed artifact cannot contain the SHA of the commit that carries it, and a later re-binding is not a re-measurement.") (severity . "moderate") (summary . "The two new captures name head 9841fed8f, but the record claimed they were measured at this head, 3a3d3297f, in four separate places. No .rkt file changed between the two heads so the numbers hold, but the record's own convention, stated in its head-coherence field and applied correctly to the suite chain, is that each capture names the tree it ran on and is never upgraded to the binding head. R3-F3 was rated moderate for exactly this shape.")))) (note . "Round 7 ran to completion and returned CHANGES-REQUESTED with seven findings, all reproduced against the tree and all fixed. Its value is that it caught the REMEDIATION rather than the work: five of its seven findings were stale summary fields in these records, and it showed the round-5 and round-6 fixes for exactly that class were stale by construction - each was written in the same commit that recorded the round it referred to, so each was a round behind the moment it landed. R6-F4, R6-F5 and R6-F6 each reproduced the defect they were filed against, one round later, which is the strongest evidence yet that the defect is the hand-written number and not the number. The fix is therefore to stop restating the count: the evidence status and the validation notes now name this record as the authority and say nothing that can fall behind, and this verdict's counts are derived from the findings it contains. The remaining two findings were real measurement errors - the manifest totals were not updated when the captures grew the manifest, and the chain and head-coherence enumerations were not updated when the same captures were added - and both are now measured against the ranges the merge candidate actually spans. R7-F7 caught the record claiming the new captures were measured at the binding head when they name an earlier one, which is this campaign's own rule, restated after being broken.") (reviewed-sha . "3a3d3297fe5172c26303a159a67a187e4639a459") (reviewer . "zai-coding-plan/glm-5.3-flash (independent, read-only)") (round . 7) (verdict . "CHANGES-REQUESTED")))) (schema-version . 2) (scope . "W7 blocked-wave repair, bake and v1.00.31 release, reviewed read-only against the frozen W7 wave doc in the campaign plan snapshot. Rounds 1-4 covered the runner base-dir fix and its regression tests, the three classes of version-coincidence defect, the W2 gate-integrity repair and its red-first proof, the W6 rehearsal matrix regeneration and head re-stamp, the W4 local-capture correction, the release honesty of the CHANGELOG entry and the release report, and the coherence and substantiation of the W7 evidence captures. Each round was a fresh read-only reviewer at the then-current head; no finding was accepted without being reproduced against the tree first.") (timestamp . "2026-09-25T17:10:00Z (r1) / 2026-09-25T17:35:00Z (r2) / 2026-09-25T20:20:00Z (r3) / 2026-09-25T22:30:00Z (r4) / 2026-09-26T02:05:00Z (r5, zai-coding-plan/glm-5.3-flash) / 2026-09-26T04:20:00Z (r6, zai-coding-plan/glm-5.3-flash)") (tooling-notes . "Round 3 was obtained on a later attempt after three provider failures: a usage-limit error on the reviewer role's default model, an OpenRouter credit limit (402) on an alternative, and an OpenRouter monthly key limit (403) on a third. Round 5 was first attempted on the routes that had served rounds 3 and 4 and could not finish: all four configured providers were quota-exhausted, the last returning a five-hour usage limit partway through. That attempt produced no verdict and is recorded as such. Round 5 was subsequently run to completion through zai-coding-plan/glm-5.3-flash and returned CHANGES-REQUESTED with nine findings, all fixed, as was round 6. The earlier wording here said round 5 could not run without qualification, which stopped being true when that round completed; the failed attempt and the completed round are now distinguished rather than conflated. No verdict was invented in place of any of these failures. The pattern across all of them is the same and is worth stating plainly: a review that cannot run is a missing gate, never an implicit approval, and the evidence record says so in its status field.") (verdict . "CHANGES-REQUESTED (rounds 1-7; all 47 findings reproduced against the tree and fixed); round 8 PENDING - NOT APPROVED, and this record must not be read as approval"))
